.TH AITERM 1 "2026-10-23" "aiterm 0.9.13-epsilon" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aiterm \- AI-assisted GTK terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aiterm
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aiterm
is a GTK3 terminal application built around a terminal pane and an AI
assistant pane. It integrates configurable AI providers, session history,
terminal-output capture, optional AI-assisted command execution, and
administrative tools for noise filtering, policies, and SNMP telemetry.
.PP
The application uses VTE for terminal emulation and MariaDB for persistent
history and related state. An AI provider and database may require separate
configuration. The application can start only when its network-availability
check succeeds, unless the relevant offline override is enabled in the
running build.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Print command-line help and application highlights, then exit.
.TP
.B --version
Print version, build identifier, and build time, then exit.
.TP
.B --debug
Enable verbose diagnostic output on standard error. This also prints version
information.
.TP
.B --color
Enable colorized diagnostic output when appropriate.
.TP
.B --bw
Force black-and-white diagnostic output.
.TP
.B --features
Print the built-in feature and release information, then exit.
.TP
.B --highlights
Print application highlights, then exit.
.TP
.B --directives
Print the general AI directives, then exit.
.TP
.B --provider
Load configuration and print the active provider, model, protocol, base URL,
and endpoint, then exit.
.TP
.B --list-models
List Gemini models. A master encryption key is required.
.TP
.BI --master= key
Supply the master key used to decrypt configured credentials. The key may
instead be supplied through AITERM_MASTER_KEY.
.TP
.BI --crypt-pw= text
Encrypt a plaintext secret and print the encrypted representation. Requires
a master key through --master or AITERM_MASTER_KEY.
.TP
.B --decrypt-pw
Print decrypted provider credentials and the database password. Use only in a
trusted terminal because secrets are exposed in diagnostic output.
.SH FEATURES
.SS Terminal and AI pane
The main window provides a terminal and an AI pane. The AI pane can receive
questions and selected application context. The interface supports multiple
terminal tabs and session-aware behavior.
.SS AI providers
Provider configuration supports OpenAI-compatible APIs and Gemini, plus
configured provider options including Groq, OpenRouter, Mistral, Claude, Ollama,
and a custom provider. Availability depends on the configured endpoint, model, and
credentials. See
.BR aiterm.conf (5).
.SS Capture and automation
Tee mode captures terminal output for application context and history. Auto
Reply analyzes captured output. AI payload auto-execution can submit approved
or permitted command payloads to the execution workflow; use policy controls
carefully and review commands before enabling automation.
.SS History and sessions
AITerm can persist session history and context in MariaDB. Session and history
managers provide access to saved records. Global-context read and write toggles
control whether the corresponding global context streams are used.
.SS Additional tools
The application includes provider and API-key managers, noise filtering,
smart caching, request-rate limiting, AI retry controls, export and printing,
XML payload tagging, and SNMP monitoring and command management.
.SS Idle suspension
Idle suspension temporarily disables selected background/runtime toggles after
a configured period without user activity, then restores their previous states
when activity resumes. Configure idle_enabled and idle_timeout_minutes in the
configuration file.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
Commands are entered in the AI input line. A leading slash is optional.
Command matching is case-insensitive and uses prefix matching against the
command registry, so use the full command words to avoid ambiguous matches.
See
.BR aiterm-commands (7)
for a categorized reference.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AITERM_CONFIG
Use this configuration path when it names an existing file.
.TP
.B AITERM_MASTER_KEY
Fallback master key for encrypted configuration values.
.TP
.B AITERM_SQL_DIR
Override the directory containing SQL schema initialization scripts, when the
specified directory exists.
.TP
.B AITERM_DEBUG
Set initial debug mode (1 or 0).
.TP
.B AITERM_COLOR
Set initial colorized diagnostic output (1 or 0).
.TP
.B AITERM_PROVIDER
Override the configured provider name.
.TP
.B AITERM_MODEL
Override the model name.
.TP
.B AITERM_PROVIDER_BASE_URL, AITERM_PROVIDER_ENDPOINT
Override provider transport URL and endpoint.
.TP
.B AITERM_PROVIDER_AUTH_HEADER, AITERM_PROVIDER_AUTH_SCHEME, AITERM_PROVIDER_QUERY_KEY
Override provider authentication transport settings.
.TP
.B AITERM_<CONFIG_KEY>
Ordinary configuration values can be overridden using the uppercase key name
prefixed with AITERM_, for example AITERM_IDLE_ENABLED or
AITERM_TERM_TRANSPARENCY. Overrides are runtime-only and are not saved back to
the configuration file. The current loader applies these overrides while
processing configuration entries, so ensure the corresponding key exists in
the file.
.TP
.B <PROVIDER>_KEY, <PROVIDER>_API_KEY
Provider-specific credential fallback variables, for example GEMINI_KEY or
OPENAI_API_KEY. These are distinct from encrypted credential fields.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/aiterm.conf
System-wide fallback configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/aiterm.conf
Per-user configuration file, preferred over ~/.aiterm.conf when present.
.TP
.I ~/.aiterm.conf
Legacy per-user configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/.UID.aiterm.conf
Per-user configuration file in /etc, where UID is the numeric user ID.
.TP
.I /usr/share/aiterm/db/
Default SQL schema directory; installation paths may be customized at build
or runtime.
.SH SECURITY
Provider API keys and the database password are stored as encrypted values in
the configuration file. Protect the master key and configuration file.
Avoid --decrypt-pw in shared terminals or logs. Environment variables may be
visible to processes or diagnostic tooling depending on system configuration.
AI-assisted execution can run terminal commands; enable it only when its
policy and approval behavior are understood.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B aiterm --version
Display build information.
.TP
.B AITERM_MASTER_KEY='secret' aiterm --provider
Inspect the selected provider configuration.
.TP
.B AITERM_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MINUTES=15 aiterm
Run with a 15-minute idle timeout when the corresponding configuration entry
is present.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aiterm.conf (5),
.BR aiterm-commands (7),
.BR man (1)
